{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:08:47.361Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implementation** (`src/cli/approve.ts`):\n- Empty-ids check now throws `CommandError` instead of `console.error` + `process.exit(1)`.\n- No-terminal `review` branch throws `CommandError(refusalMessage(...))`.\n- Per-id `catch` rethrows `CommandError` unchanged; otherwise prints nothing and throws `CommandError('Error approving <id>:\\n  <message>', { next })`, where `next` is the computed next step when `findChange`/`readNextStep` succeed.\n\n**Tests**:\n- `tests/approve-confirm.test.ts` and `tests/plan-approve-next-step.test.ts`: only `captureExitAndLogs` changed to catch `CommandError` and read `exitCode`/message/`next`; titles and assertions untouched.\n- New `tests/command-error-approve.test.ts`: template approval, error-before-next ordering, missing change, several-ids stop-at-first-failure, and unwrapped `--confirm` refusal, all through `runCliCaptured`.\n- New `tests/cli-no-process-exit.test.ts`: recursively fails naming any `src/cli/*.ts` containing `process.exit(`.\n\n**Verification**: task verify passes (6/6), related approve tests pass (37/37), and the proposal verify `pnpm verify` exits 0 (typechecks, build, full suite, lint).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/111-commands-throw/.run/results/4.md`."}}
